  "raw_label": "1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "K.Kavitha vs The State Of Telangana on 16 February, 2022",
    "facts": "This writ petition is filed by mother of the detenue, challenging the order of detention dated 15.10.2021, in exercise of the power under Section 3(2) of the Telangana Prevention of Dangerous Activities of Bootleggers, Dacoits, Drug-Offenders, Goondas, Immoral Traffic Offenders, Land Grabbers, Spurious Seed Offenders, Insecticide Offenders, Fertiliser Offenders, Food Adulteration Offenders, Fake Document Offenders, Scheduled Commodities Offenders, Forest Offenders, Gaming Offenders, Sexual Offenders, Explosive Substances Offenders, Arms Offenders, Cyber Crime Offenders and While Collar or Financial Offenders Act, 1986 (Act 1 of 1986). 4. The order of detention refers to four offences stated to have been committed by detenue on 12.04.2021. These crimes were registered against detenue under Sections 395 and 394 respectively, in Intezargunj Police Station and Hasanparthy Police Station respectively. 5. It was alleged that detenue with three other co-accused resorted to dacoity on highways. Such action of the detenue disturbs public order and if he was left scot-free, he would indulge in committing similar crimes affecting general public, causing fear and apprehension on people travelling on the road covering limits of these two police stations. The order of detention was made after bail was granted by the competent Court. During the period from 2010 to 2020, he was involved in 27 offences. Holding that on the crimes alleged against the detenue, preventive detention was not warranted, this Court allowed the writ petition.",
    "arguments": "6. Learned counsel for the petitioner submits that the crimes registered against detenue were ordinary crimes which could be prosecuted under criminal procedure code and do not require taking recourse to preventive detention. 7. It is appropriate to note that the detenue was not involved in any other crimes of similar nature earlier and all the four crimes were stated to have been occurred on the very same day. 8. The learned counsel for the petitioner places reliance on the decision of this Court in W.P.No.9334 of 2021. In the said case, detenue was treated as a 'Goonda' as he was alleged to have been involved in robbery at Singareni Collieries Company Limited in the limits of Ramagundam Police Commissionerate.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "6. Learned counsel for the petitioner submits that the crimes registered against detenue were ordinary crimes which could be prosecuted under criminal procedure code and do not require taking recourse to preventive detention. 7. It is appropriate to note that the detenue was not involved in any other crimes of similar nature earlier and all the four crimes were stated to have been occurred on the very same day. 8. The learned counsel for the petitioner places reliance on the decision of this Court in W.P.No.9334 of 2021. In the said case, detenue was treated as a 'Goonda' as he was alleged to have been involved in robbery at Singareni Collieries Company Limited in the limits of Ramagundam Police Commissionerate.",
    "respondent_arguments": "",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": ""
